From e7ee6bee60db12114c77093036a8b4f8efabc57a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: zhengwenming <zhengwenming@apexsoft.com.cn>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 03:06:14 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] server: make a dma-buf import of a compressed export ask for
 the export's size

Mali r56 lays an AFBC image out with the superblock row pitch (1668x2173 BGRA8:
27,648) and answers that pitch from vkGetImageSubresourceLayout, while the memory
requirement is the 16x16 superblocks' payload (3,760,128 bytes). An importer that
passes the layout back while naming DRM_FORMAT_MOD_LINEAR has the pitch read as a
pixel row's: 27,648 x 2172 + 6,672 = 60,058,128 bytes asked of a 3,760,128-byte
dma-buf, and vkAllocateMemory fails with VK_ERROR_INVALID_EXTERNAL_HANDLE (-1000072003).
Zink loses the surface and Gecko falls back to wl_shm. The explicit AFBC modifier
with the full layout is refused by the driver outright
(VK_ERROR_INVALID_DRM_FORMAT_MODIFIER_PLANE_LAYOUT_EXT).

The server now remembers the shape and plane layout of the dma-buf exports it made
(server_dmabuf_meta.c) and, when an import carries one of them, creates the image at
the export's modifier without the explicit plane layout: the driver lays it out as
the exporter did, vkGetImageMemoryRequirements matches the dma-buf, and the layout
and modifier answers stay the exporter's. LINEAR exports are not remembered - their
importers are right about LINEAR - and the client is unchanged.

tests/dbmeta_unit.c covers the register and runs in host/run_ci_tests.sh.
docs/afbc-dmabuf-import.md has the measurements, a no-application reproduction and
the remaining exporter-side boundary (Zen's wl_buffer names LINEAR with the
compressed stride; the compositor then refuses it).
